## Original Content
"Pizza Pod started with a pretty ridiculous idea: What if I could turn a tiny Smart car into a mobile pizzeria?" says founder Bradley Alvelo.

## Summary
Bradley Alvelo, a 38-year-old entrepreneur, founded Pizza Pod, a mobile pizzeria operating out of a tiny Smart car in New York City. He describes the unconventional setup as being 'like a circus or a magic act,' turning a seemingly ridiculous idea into a functioning food business.

## Key Points
- Pizza Pod is a mobile pizzeria operated out of a compact Smart car in New York City
- Founder Bradley Alvelo conceived the business from what he calls 'a pretty ridiculous idea'
- The 38-year-old founder compares running the operation to 'a circus or a magic act' due to its unconventional nature
- The venture demonstrates how creative adaptation of small vehicles can enable food entrepreneurship in dense urban environments


